"A Seal cleanses mana; a corrupted Seal corrupts it instead."
"A Seal has a wizardry switch that sets it to purify magic or to corrupt it."
"Corrupting a Seal is simple, and the blight then fights anyone who tries to fix it."
"A blighted Seal releases only its corrupt mana type, such as death mana."
"Corrupting one Seal subverts some share of all the mana in Davrar."
"The blights were meant as challenges, dungeons for Questors to conquer."
"A blightmind is thousands of gigantic death elementals fed by the Seal beneath them."
"A blightmind attacks with fear, wizardry and twists of reality."
"The blightmind's tendrils talk by passing mana where they touch."
"Blighted death Seals are called undead Seals, always a caustic burn."
"A Conclave vote could fix all the blights at once."
"Later, the Helmaris blight is cleared by five people outside a Solstice."
"Its Seal's switch had been disconnected, with death-mana tendrils gripping its workings."
"Later, bone obelisks pull all the death mana for miles into one mountain-levelling torrent."
"Later, the Heirs' first deed conquers Esebus and their second clears the Helmaris blight."
"Vesh, Sarya's teacher, has killed twenty-three blights."
"Brox once smashed an undead blight at Itonia; Badud annihilated one in Quilbor."
"Years later, the Continuance Charter aims for blights with agency of their own."
